{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>When it goes out in the Jubilee.</b> Scripture mentioned this regarding every field, for in the Jubilee it goes out." "<b>Like a devoted field.</b> That he vows a vow to devote it too to the priest, and he who valuates is the priest, for it is 'he who valuates' [העריך], and there is no need for him to be a high priest."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {1 "The phrase 'for it is העריך' likely echoes Leviticus 27:18 (העריך הכהן) where the plain priest, not the high priest, performs valuation; preserved Ibn Ezra's compressed syntax rather than expanding."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:13:00.350003632Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}